		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=13173#p13173"><![CDATA[
The best bet right now is Blender, it has Bullet integrated and allows to setup collision shapes, rigid body and constraints, as well as run the simulation.<br>There are some books on how to use Bullet inside Blender with examples, such as 'bounce, tumble and splash' by Tony Mullen.<br><br>The Dynamica Maya plugin can do the same, except for constraint support (it is work-in-progress).<br>What kind of editor do you have in mind? Which platform?<br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Fri Apr 03, 2009 7:14 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
